stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Probe
    Probe --> Begin: active or idle front / actor grant recheck
    Begin --> Closing: durable journal and exact old identity
    Closing --> CloseHeld: close failed / no old keys
    CloseHeld --> Closing: backoff wake and fresh identity check
    Closing --> Checking: same control connection / kill exact pane
    Checking --> Ended: provider identity positively absent
    Ended --> Bound: latest durable native ID / existing resume guards
    Bound --> FirstHeld: composer pre-key refusal / typed Held and proof
    FirstHeld --> Bound: level screen wake / same queued original
    Bound --> Reserved: existing composer and owner gate
    Reserved --> MayHaveSent: durable Bootstrap commit
    MayHaveSent --> Effect: backend keys
    Effect --> Receipt: durable native receipt / owner observes it
    Receipt --> Done: exact attempt settlement
    Done --> Complete: no owed original
    MayHaveSent --> Unknown: daemon crash before first key
    Effect --> Unknown: daemon crash before receipt settlement
    Unknown --> Retained: existing main tick / Unconfirmed
    Retained --> Complete: original in retained once / no live journal
    Begin --> Cancelled: explicit cancel or clear
    FirstHeld --> Cancelled: explicit cancel or clear
    Cancelled --> Complete: no owed original
    state Restart {
        [*] --> Census: input OR unfinished journal
        Census --> Awake: explicit boot wake
        Awake --> Closing: unfinished old close
        Awake --> Complete: Bound and original no longer owed
    }
    note right of CloseHeld
      Fixed unread screen and permanent close failure preserve Held.
      No close-success fairness; no old fallback, C-s, or old payload.
    end note
    note right of Closing
      Same tmux control connection and exact pane metadata.
      EOF discards authority; no PID signal or blind number replay.
      Close acknowledgment does not prove transcript flush.
    end note
    note right of FirstHeld
      Existing composer/Person draft guard remains.
      Positive no-key proof reaches hold_not_sent and wake.
      No native-first capability in slice A.
    end note
    note right of Unknown
      Accepted crash exception: main Bootstrap to Unknown to retained.
      NoRetained covers crash-free executions.
      Unknown is never blindly replayed.
    end note
    Complete --> [*]
